  },
  {
    "@id": "http://purl.org/spar/bido-core",
    "@type": [
      "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Ontology"
    ],
    "http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/contributor": [
      {
        "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string",
        "@value": "Sebastian Barzaghi (https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0799-1527)"
      }
    ],
    "http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/creator": [
      {
        "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string",
        "@value": "Enrico Motta (https://orcid.org/0000-0003-0015-1952)"
      },
      {
        "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string",
        "@value": "Francesco Osborne (https://orcid.org/0000-0001-6557-3131)"
      },
      {
        "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string",
        "@value": "Silvio Peroni (http://orcid.org/0000-0003-0530-4305)"
      }
    ],
    "http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/date": [
      {
        "@value": "2026-08-14"
      }
    ],
    "http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "\nThe core module of BiDO allows us to describe any entity and the related bibliometric data (through the property `bido:holdsBibliometricDataInTime`) at a certain time (i.e., `tvc:atTime`, a property defined by the imported TVC ontology for specifying temporal instants or intervals) and according to a certain agent (through the property `bido:accordingTo`, which is a sub-property of `prov:wasAttributedTo` and allows us to indicate the agent responsible for such bibliometric data).\n\n![The architecture of the BiDO-Core module.](bido-core.png)\n\nTwo alternative kinds of bibliometric data are specifiable (through the property `bido:withBibliometricData`) in BiDO: numeric data and categorial data. \nNumeric data are those characterised by a certain integer or float value related to a particular bibliometric measure. \nSome of these measures – i.e., h-index, author citation count, e-index, and journal impact factor – are available in a particular module of BiDO responsible for describing the most common bibliometric measures.\n"
      }
    ],
    "http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/title": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "BiDO Core module (BiDO-Core)"
      }
    ],
    "http://purl.org/dc/terms/bibliographicCitation": [
      {
        "@value": "Osborne, F., Peroni, S., Motta, E. (2014). Clustering Citation Distributions for Semantic Categorization and Citation Prediction. In Proceedings of the 4th Workshop on Linked Science (LISC 2014): 24–35. http://ceur-ws.org/Vol-1282/lisc2014_submission_9.pdf"
      }
    ],
